{
  "about": [
    "The rules for filtering and sorting tasks, as cases that every implementation must pass:",
    "src/query.js (test/query.test.js), the command-line client's port and the iPhone app's port.",
    "Each task is `defaults` with its own fields on top. A case uses the task set named by `tasks`",
    "(board when it names none) and `today` (the top-level one when it gives none). `filter` holds",
    "text exactly as GET /api/v1/tasks takes it; a field left out does not narrow the list, and no",
    "status means every status. `sort` is the text form (no sort means the default order). `expect`",
    "is the ids in order. A case with `view` is a named view instead, and expects its groups. A case",
    "with `error` expects parsing to fail: the sort, or the filter."
  ],
